Subject: [PATCH] NetworkPkg/DxeNetLib: no ASSERT when EFI_RNG_PROTOCOL is absent

PseudoRandom (and PseudoRandomU32, through it) documents EFI_NOT_FOUND
for "RNG protocol not found", and each of its 20 call sites at the tag,
all in NetworkPkg, checks the status and returns it (iSCSI's CHAP
breaks out of its exchange). Those on a driver's Start path (Ip4Dxe
and Ip6Dxe's DriverBindingStart, Dhcp4Dxe, Dhcp6Dxe and Ip6Dxe's
service creation, UefiPxeBcDxe's IPv6 children) then fail the start,
and a later ConnectController starts the driver again; those in an
entry point (Udp4Dxe, Udp6Dxe, TcpDxe) run only once the Depex below
is met. But a DEBUG build also asserted there, and with
PcdDebugPropertyMask's deadloop the machine stopped.

The library's Depex on gEfiRngProtocolGuid holds the network drivers
back only until they are dispatched. After that an RNG produced by a
driver-model driver can be absent while they start: the Shell's
`reconnect -r` disconnects every driver, VirtioRngDxe's included, and
connects the network controllers before the virtio-rng device, so on a
CPU with no RNG instruction (QEMU's AARCH64 cortex-a57, no FEAT_RNG;
X64 without RDRAND), where virtio-rng is the only EFI_RNG_PROTOCOL,
Ip4DriverBindingStart asserted at DxeNetLib.c(944). A RELEASE build
already went on: the drivers whose start failed were started again
later in the same `reconnect -r`, and the network worked.

Drop that one ASSERT_EFI_ERROR, keeping its DEBUG_ERROR message. The
ASSERTs on GetRNG failures stay: there an RNG exists and failed.
RELEASE builds compile no ASSERT, so they are unchanged.

axl-firmware's patch against edk2-stable202611, applied after
0014-aarch64-tpm-pei-map.patch to a copy of the packages it touches.

---
diff --git a/NetworkPkg/Library/DxeNetLib/DxeNetLib.c b/NetworkPkg/Library/DxeNetLib/DxeNetLib.c
index 5c7ea0c..963fc9b 100644
--- a/NetworkPkg/Library/DxeNetLib/DxeNetLib.c
+++ b/NetworkPkg/Library/DxeNetLib/DxeNetLib.c
@@ -940,8 +940,13 @@ PseudoRandom (
 
   Status = gBS->LocateProtocol (&gEfiRngProtocolGuid, NULL, (VOID **)&RngProtocol);
   if (EFI_ERROR (Status)) {
+    //
+    // Not an assertion: a caller may run before any RNG producer is
+    // connected (a reconnect stops a driver-model RNG such as
+    // VirtioRngDxe with every other driver), and every caller returns the
+    // error, so a later ConnectController retries it.
+    //
     DEBUG ((DEBUG_ERROR, "Failed to locate EFI_RNG_PROTOCOL: %r\n", Status));
-    ASSERT_EFI_ERROR (Status);
     return Status;
   }
 
